---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import VGISubNav from '../../components/sections/VGISubNav.astro';
import PageHead from '../../components/ui/PageHead.astro';
import Button from '../../components/ui/Button.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/ui/CodeBlock.astro';
import AgentQuickstart from '../../components/vgi/AgentQuickstart.astro';
import AgentBuildProof from '../../components/vgi/AgentBuildProof.astro';
import AgentCsvExample from '../../components/vgi/AgentCsvExample.astro';
import RecordedAgentBuild from '../../components/vgi/RecordedAgentBuild.astro';
import VgiWalkthroughVideo from '../../components/vgi/VgiWalkthroughVideo.astro';
import { vgiSkillsFile } from '../../lib/vgi-agents';
import { organization } from '../../lib/organization';
const description = 'Your coding agent can build and test a VGI worker today. See a real prompt become a DuckDB function, then build one in your own language.';
const jsonLd = [{ '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'TechArticle', headline: 'Your coding agent can build your next DuckDB function', description, url: 'https://query.farm/vgi/build-with-an-agent', author: organization }, { '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'BreadcrumbList', itemListElement: [{ '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'VGI', item: 'https://query.farm/vgi/' }, { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Build with an Agent', item: 'https://query.farm/vgi/build-with-an-agent' }] }];
---
<PageLayout title="Build a DuckDB function with your coding agent" description={description} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <VGISubNav />
  <PageHead variant="section" eyebrow="VGI for coding agents" title="Your coding agent can build your next DuckDB function." titleClass="mt-3 max-w-[25ch] text-4xl md:text-5xl text-soil-900" ledeClass="mt-4 max-w-[79ch] text-base sm:text-lg leading-relaxed text-soil-700" hairband>
    <Fragment slot="lede">Describe what you need and choose your language. With the VGI skill, your agent writes a worker, runs it through DuckDB, and checks the results. You keep the source and tests.</Fragment>
    <div class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap gap-3"><Button href="#start" variant="primary" size="md">Build one with your agent →</Button><Button href="#watch" variant="secondary" size="md">Watch a real build</Button></div>
    <AgentBuildProof />
  </PageHead>

  <section class="section-container py-9 sm:py-11">
    <p class="max-w-[85ch] leading-relaxed text-soil-700"><strong class="text-soil-900">VGI is the DuckDB extension. The worker is the program your agent builds.</strong> It exposes your code as SQL functions. This first function turns text into URL slugs; it is deliberately small so you can inspect the agent’s work.</p>
    <div class="mt-8"><AgentQuickstart /></div>
    <p class="mt-5 max-w-[90ch] text-sm leading-relaxed text-soil-600">Have your coding agent and chosen language runtime ready. The installer uses Node.js; SQL verification uses <a href="https://docs.astral.sh/uv/" class="text-link underline">uv</a> and stock DuckDB. Live builds have been tested with Codex and Claude Code. Cursor, Copilot, and OpenCode have installation checks. <a href={vgiSkillsFile('evals/RESULTS.md')} class="text-link underline">Compatibility details →</a></p>
  </section>

  <section class="section-container py-9 sm:py-12" id="use-it"><AgentCsvExample /></section>
  <section class="section-container py-9 sm:py-12" id="watch"><VgiWalkthroughVideo /></section>

  <section class="section-container py-9 sm:py-12" id="next">
    <div class="max-w-[78ch]"><h2 class="text-3xl text-soil-900">The next function can be yours.</h2><p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-soil-700">You could implement this small slug function in SQL. The useful next step is to expose a function or package your project already maintains: a validator, a parser, or a calculation. Tell your agent which code to wrap and which results it must verify.</p><p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-soil-700">VGI—the Vector Gateway Interface—connects DuckDB to that worker using typed columns. Once built, DuckDB calls the worker without a coding agent in the request path. Workers can also expose <a href="/vgi/building-a-worker" class="text-link underline">tables and catalogs</a>.</p><p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-soil-700">But a new library brings new edge cases. Keep the SQL tests, add representative inputs, and ask the agent to rerun them as the worker grows. <a href={vgiSkillsFile('examples/shipping-margin/README.md')} class="text-link underline">Explore a larger worked example →</a></p></div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-container pb-12" id="proof">
    <details class="rounded-xl border border-soil-300 p-5 sm:p-6" data-build-evidence><summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-soil-900">Inspect the recorded builds, generated source, and timings</summary><div class="mt-8"><RecordedAgentBuild /></div></details>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[90ch] text-xs leading-relaxed text-soil-600">Recorded on macOS ARM64 with shared package caches. Some builds took more than five minutes. These are measured examples, not a completion-time guarantee. The CSV follow-on is verified separately from the original timed build.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section-container pb-16" id="engine">
    <details class="rounded-xl border border-soil-300 p-5 sm:p-6"><summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-soil-900">The DuckDB setup your agent uses</summary>
      <div class="mt-4 min-w-0 text-sm leading-relaxed text-soil-700"><p>Stock DuckDB 2.0.0 loads VGI from the signed <a href="/blog/duckdb-2-query-farm-repository/" class="text-link underline">Query Farm extension repository</a>:</p><div class="mt-4"><CodeBlock code={`SET allow_extension_repositories = 'allowed';\nCREATE EXTENSION REPOSITORY IF NOT EXISTS query_farm\n    WITH PREFIX 'https://duckdb-extensions.query.farm';\nINSTALL vgi FROM query_farm;\nLOAD vgi FROM query_farm;`} lang="sql" tryable={false} /></div><p class="mt-3">In later sessions, use <code>LOAD vgi FROM query_farm</code>. Existing Haybarn projects can keep their engine. Check the available build for your version and platform.</p></div>
    </details>
    <div class="mt-9 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-5"><Button href="#start" variant="primary">Choose your language and build →</Button><a href="/blog/build-vgi-workers-with-coding-agents/" class="text-sm text-link underline underline-offset-2">Read the build story</a></div>
  </section>
</PageLayout>
